/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/_codegen_logs/run_20260618_021006_seed1583749884/seed1583749884__16__codegen_prompts__4.log:19:{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,260p' /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/16/prompt.md && printf '\\\\n--- DES ---\\\\n' && sed -n '1,220p' /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/16/des.md\"","aggregated_output":"你是一个 ARC-AGI 谜题设计专家。下面的 20 道参考题是难度和机制质量的标杆。仔细阅读每道题的**解题逻辑**（解题者从样例归纳规则的认知过程），而非表面场景。你的新题应在机制深度和隐蔽性上与参考题持平或者实现超越。\n\n每个参考题描述包含：\n- `description`：一句话概述题目的变换目标。\n- `Input structure`：输入网格中有哪些对象、背景、标记、边界或组件。\n- `Rule`：从输入到输出的确定性变换规则。\n- `Key insight`：解题所需的核心洞见。\n\n参考题目如下：\n<reference_puzzle index=\"1\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"42f83767\" lines=\"23-39\">\n<description>\nExpand the lower color grid by replacing each pixel with its matching top stencil.\n\nInput structure\nThe input has a top legend and a lower dense color grid, separated by blank rows.\nThe legend contains left-to-right 2x2 color swatches and, to their right,\nthe same number of square neutral-color stencil masks.\n\nRule\nPair the swatches and stencil masks by left-to-right order. For every pixel in\nthe lower color grid, paste the paired stencil mask as one output block,\nrecoloring the mask pixels with that pixel's color and leaving mask holes as bg.\n\nKey insight\nThe lower grid is not copied directly; it is an index grid whose colors select\nthe stencil shape from the legend, so each input pixel becomes one square block.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"2\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"98c475bf\" lines=\"62-76\">\n<description>\nErase the complete interior glyph and expand each endpoint marker pair into its color's full glyph.\n\nInput structure\n- The grid is 20x20 with background inside two same-color full-height vertical frame bars.\n- Inside the frame there is one complete color glyph and one or more other colors appearing only as two endpoint markers in the same row.\n- Marker endpoints are always in the first and last interior columns.\n\nRule\n- Keep the vertical frame unchanged.\n- Erase any complete interior glyph.\n- For each endpoint marker pair, use that marker color's learned glyph template and anchor its horizontal bar on the marker row.\n\nKey insight\n- Color identifies which glyph shape to draw; the two endpoint pixels are not copied objects, they are anchors for reconstructing that color's full symbol.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"3\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"d753a70b\" lines=\"81-93\">\n<description>\nRed diamond outlines contract by one layer and gray diamond outlines expand by one layer while other objects stay fixed.\n\nInput structure\n- A 16x16 orange-background grid contains one-cell-thick Manhattan-diamond outlines.\n- Red and gray outlines are the changing objects; other colored diamond outlines are static.\n- Some outlines may be clipped by the grid boundary, but their visible pixels still fit a clipped Manhattan-distance contour.\nRule\n- Clear all red and gray pixels.\n- Red objects are redrawn with the same diamond center and radius minus one.\n- Gray objects are redrawn with radius plus one; an ambiguous edge-clipped growing arc continues away from the nearest perpendicular edge.\nKey insight\n- The task is not about moving whole objects: each changing object is a contour of a diamond, and the visible operation is one step of contour contraction or expansion.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"4\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"87ab05b8\" lines=\"9-24\">\n<description>\nErase all distractor pixels and expand the single red control pixel into the grid quadrant that contains it.\n\nInput structure:\n- The grid has one dominant background color.\n- Exactly one red pixel is the control pixel.\n- Other non-background pixels are distractors.\n\nRule:\n- Clear the canvas to the background color.\n- Split the grid into equal top/bottom and left/right halves.\n- Fill the quadrant containing the red control pixel with red.\n\nKey insight:\n- The red control pixel selects a whole half-grid quadrant by its row half and column half; all other foreground pixels are noise.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"5\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"df978a02\" lines=\"57-72\">\n<description>\nLet the largest center-pointing object grow outward while every other object loses its inward tip.\n\nInput structure\n- The grid has a single dominant background color and four 8-connected monochromatic foreground objects.\n- The objects surround a central background gap and point toward it from cardinal directions.\n- Exactly one object has the largest area.\n\nRule\n- Find the central background gap by minimizing aggregate distance to the four objects.\n- Recolor the nearest-to-center pixel of each non-largest object to background.\n- Add a three-pixel cap in the largest object's color on the side away from the center, centered on the shared row or column.\n\nKey insight\n- The edit is a transfer of prominence around a common center: losers retract at their tips, and the unique largest object extends outward from the center.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"6\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"981571dc\" lines=\"6-19\">\n<description>\nReconstruct a 4-way symmetric mosaic by filling missing (black) pixels.\n\nInput structure:\n- A colored grid exhibiting bilateral symmetry along both a vertical and a horizontal axis.\n- Some pixels are erased to color 0 (black), creating gaps in the pattern.\n\nRule:\n- Infer the vertical and horizontal reflection axes from the visible (non-zero) pixels.\n- For each black pixel, recover its color from the mirrored position across either axis or both.\n- When multiple mirrors yield candidates, use the majority color.\n\nKey insight: The reflection axes are not given — they must be deduced from the surviving pixels by finding the axes that best preserve the existing symmetry.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"7\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"20270e3b\" lines=\"7-21\">\n<description>\nConnect two sprites using matching connector pixels, then tight-crop.\n\nInput structure:\n- Background color `bg`, sprite color `obj`, connector color `ctrl` (small, 2 components).\n- Two main foreground sprites, plus possibly tiny detached pixels belonging to one sprite.\n\nRule:\n- Identify the **base** sprite (closest to grid top-left).\n- Translate the other sprite so its connector sits one cell above the base's connector.\n- Stamp the plug onto the base; remove connectors (recolor `ctrl` to `obj`).\n- Output is the tight crop around all non-background pixels.\n\nKey insight: The connector pixels define the unique docking point and direction.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"8\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"305b1341\" lines=\"22-37\">\n<description>\nExpand each sparse color object into a filled rectangular region using its legend-paired fill color.\n\nInput structure\nA background-color grid has a two-column legend in columns 0 and 1, starting at row 0: each row gives\na source color in the left column and that source color's fill color in the right column.  Outside the\nlegend, the foreground pixels are sparse dot objects whose colors are exactly the legend source colors.\n\nRule\nClear the legend.  For each source color, take the bbox of all of its non-legend dots, expand that bbox\nby one pixel in every direction, and fill background cells inside the expanded rectangle with the paired\nlegend fill color while preserving every original non-legend dot.\n\nKey insight\nThe legend order is also the layer order: earlier legend rows are in front, so fill rectangles are painted\nfrom the last legend row back to the first and higher-priority fills overwrite lower-priority fills.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"9\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"1d61978c\" lines=\"8-22\">\n<description>\nRecolor the two diagonal foreground-bar orientations, assigning teal to the larger orientation and red to the smaller one.\n\nInput structure\n- The grid has one dominant background color and one foreground color.\n- Foreground pixels form one-cell-thick diagonal bars.\n- Every foreground pixel belongs to exactly one diagonal orientation.\n\nRule\n- Keep the background unchanged.\n- Classify each foreground pixel by whether it has a diagonal neighbor on the NW/SE axis or the NE/SW axis.\n- Recolor the orientation with more foreground pixels teal and the other orientation red.\n\nKey insight\n- The output colors depend on the relative population of the two diagonal orientations, not on a fixed slash direction or position.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"10\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"ecb67b6d\" lines=\"138-155\">\n<description>\nRecolor the grey diagonal-chain regions in an orange field to teal.\n\nInput structure\nThe input contains only grey pixels and orange pixels.  Grey pixels form\nseveral 8-connected regions embedded in the orange field.\n\nRule\nDecompose each grey 8-connected region into 4-connected lobes.  Recolor the\nwhole region teal only when it contains a straight diagonal run of at least\nthree pixels and those lobes meet only by diagonal corner contacts in a\nnon-branching diagonal chain or cycle; a single 4-connected region is\nrecolored only when it is a square diagonal staircase.\n\nKey insight\nThe teal regions are not selected by size or position; they are the grey\nregions whose internal connectivity depends on diagonal corner joins, while\nsame-edge cracks, rectangles, bars, and branching/noisy regions remain grey.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"11\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"a1aa0c1e\" lines=\"74-97\">\n<description>\nCompress the stacked colored bars into a compact ordered table with the control pixel on the selected row.\n\nInput structure\n- A background grid contains several full-width colored bars from top to\n  bottom; the last bar is the base/separator color.\n- Each non-base bar may have an aligned three-column comb motif below it,\n  alternating side-pair rows with solid rows.\n- A singleton control pixel sits away from the colored motifs.\n\nRule\n- Make one output row per non-base bar, preserving top-to-bottom order.\n- In that row, paint the bar color once for each solid three-pixel row in\n  its motif, then paint the base-bar color in the separator column.\n- The singleton control pixel sits immediately above the base bar. Among\n  motifs whose open side-pair parity is compatible with that bottom row,\n  put the control pixel in the output row with the fewest solid rows; use\n  horizontal distance to the motif center only to break count ties.\n\nKey insight\n- The vertical comb height is a count, while the control pixel is read by\n  projecting it onto the center gap of compatible comb rows rather than by\n  its vertical band alone.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"12\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"b10624e5\" lines=\"24-39\">\n<description>\nReplicate a motif across quadrants with scaling and reflection keyed to red anchor blocks.\n\nInput structure:\n- Grid divided into four quadrants by a full-row and full-column divider of a single non-bg color.\n- Each quadrant contains a red (2) square anchor block of varying size.\n- The top-left quadrant also has a colored motif attached to its red anchor.\n\nRule:\n- Use the top-left quadrant's motif as the source pattern.\n- For each other quadrant, scale the motif by the ratio of that quadrant's red block size to the source red block size.\n- Reflect horizontally for right-side quadrants, vertically for bottom quadrants (both for bottom-right).\n- Align the scaled/reflected motif so its red region overlaps the target anchor, then stamp non-bg pixels.\n\nKey insight: Red block size encodes the scale factor; quadrant position encodes the reflection axes.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"13\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"15660dd6\" lines=\"33-54\">\n<description>\nCombine each column's repeated template mask with its single solid color swatch.\n\nInput structure:\n- The grid is a table of framed panels separated by background rows/columns.\n- The leftmost column gives one solid row-label color for each panel row.\n- In each panel column, exactly one panel has a solid non-background interior,\n  while the other panels share the same mask drawn in one template color on\n  the background.\n\nRule:\n- For every panel column, find the row containing the solid interior swatch.\n- Rebuild one output panel using that row's left label as the frame color.\n- Fill the repeated template mask with the swatch color and leave the mask\n\n--- DES ---\n<new_puzzle>\n- `description`：将网格中每个前景对象的像素按行扫描顺序重新排列为底部对齐的垂直条，条的列位置由对象颜色在图例中的排名决定。\n\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 背景为 Black。\n  - 网格最左列有一个垂直颜色图例：从上到下排列不同颜色的像素（如 Red、Blue、Green、Yellow），代表列位置 0、1、2、3。\n  - 网格中散布着若干个 4-连通单色前景对象（颜色与图例中的颜色匹配），面积各不相同。\n\n- `Rule`：\n  - 创建与输入同大的背景色画布。\n  - 对每种图例颜色，计算该颜色在网格中的总像素数 N。\n  - 在图例中找到该颜色的排名 K（从上到下第 K 个）。\n  - 在输出画布的第 K 列中，从底部向上绘制 N 个该颜色的像素。\n  - 保持图例列不变。\n\n- `Key insight`：对象的形状和位置被完全丢弃，仅保留像素总数作为条的高度；图例既定义了颜色到列位置的映射，又隐含了多种颜色共存时的排列规则。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n<new_puzzle>\n- `description`：在两个半面板中，找到能够完美\"拼合\"为矩形的对象对，将它们移动到彼此相邻的位置并合并。\n\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 背景为 Azure。\n  - 网格被一条完整的 Maroon 水平分隔线分为上下两个面板。\n  - 上面板有 2-3 个 4-连通单色前景对象，下面板也有 2-3 个 4-连通单色前景对象。\n  - 上面板中的每个对象与下面板中的恰好一个对象可以拼合为一个完整的矩形（两者的形状互补：将一个翻转后放在另一个旁边恰好填满一个矩形）。\n\n- `Rule`：\n  - 对每对上下面板的对象，测试是否存在一种拼合方式使两者形成完整矩形（允许垂直翻转下面板对象）。\n  - 找到所有匹配的对象对。\n  - 在输出中，将每对匹配对象拼合为矩形绘制，矩形之间间隔一列背景色，从左到右按上面板对象的原始列位置排列。\n  - 上面板对象保持原色在上方，下面板对象保持原色在下方。\n  - 丢弃分隔线。\n\n- `Key insight`：配对基于形状互补性（拼合为矩形），而非颜色或大小匹配——解题者需要在心理上\"翻转拼合\"来验证每对候选对象。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n<new_puzzle>\n- `description`：根据每个对象边界上 Yellow 标记像素的数量和位置，在对象的对应方向上绘制等长的射线。\n\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 背景为 Black。\n  - 网格中有若干个 4-连通的 Grey 实心前景对象。\n  - 每个对象的边界上有 1-4 个 Yellow 标记像素（替换了该位置的 Grey 像素），分布在对象的不同边上。\n\n- `Rule`：\n  - 对每个 Yellow 标记像素，确定它所在的对象边（上/下/左/右边界）。\n  - 从标记位置沿着远离对象的方向（即标记所在边的法线外方向）绘制一条 Yellow 射线。\n  - 射线长度等于该对象的 Yellow 标记总数。\n  - 射线不覆盖已有的前景像素。\n  - 保持对象的 Grey 像素不变。\n\n- `Key insight`：每个标记的方向由其所在的边决定，而所有标记的射线长度相同（等于标记总数）——标记总数同时编码了射线长度，形成了一种\"自计数\"机制。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n<new_puzzle>\n- `description`：将网格中每一行的前景像素按颜色分组后向两侧推离，颜色在图例中的排名决定了推离的优先级。\n\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 背景为 Black。\n  - 网格最上行有一个颜色优先级图例：从左到右排列不同颜色像素（如 Red、Blue、Green），越靠左优先级越高。\n  - 网格下方各行中包含不同颜色的前景像素，混合在同一行中。\n\n- `Rule`：\n  - 对每行（图例行除外），收集所有前景像素。\n  - 按颜色在图例中的优先级排序：最高优先级的颜色像素放在行的中心，次高优先级的像素向两侧扩展，最低优先级的像素被推到行的两端。\n  - 具体地：最高优先级的像素保持在原行的中心区域（居中放置），次优先级的像素紧贴在其两侧，以此类推。\n  - 每种颜色的像素保持原有数量，在其分配的区域内居中排列。\n\n- `Key insight`：优先级不是决定\"去留\"而是决定\"位置\"——高优先级的颜色占据中心，低优先级的被推到边缘；这是一种基于排名的空间重分配。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n<new_puzzle>\n- `description`：在包含\"时钟面板\"序列的网格中，每个面板的指针位置相对于前一个面板顺时针旋转了固定角度；补全最后一个缺失指针的面板。\n\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 背景为 Black。\n  - 网格被 Grey 分隔列分为 4 个等大的正方形面板。\n  - 每个面板中心有一个 Red 像素（圆心），周围有一个由 Grey 像素构成的 5x5 正方形边框（表盘）。\n  - 前 3 个面板中，各有一个 Yellow 的 2 像素长指针从中心向边框延伸，指向 8 个方向之一（上、右上、右、右下、下、左下、左、左上）。\n  - 第 4 个面板只有表盘和圆心，没有指针。\n\n- `Rule`：\n  - 观察前 3 个面板的指针方向序列，推断相邻面板间的固定旋转步长（每步 = 45 度顺时针旋转 K 步，K 为常数）。\n  - 将第 3 个面板的指针方向再顺时针旋转 K 步，得到第 4 个面板的指针方向。\n  - 在第 4 个面板中绘制该方向的 Yellow 指针。\n\n- `Key insight`：面板序列是一个旋转动画的帧；旋转步长需要从前三帧中归纳——这是一种序列外推任务，核心推理在于发现恒定的旋转增量。\n</new_puzzle>\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/_codegen_logs/run_20260618_021006_seed1583749884/seed1583749884__16__codegen_prompts__4.log:22:{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '68,220p' /home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/e3721c99.py && sed -n '600,790p' /home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/e3721c99.py\"","aggregated_output":"def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n    \"\"\"\n    Recolor grey shapes by matching their hole count to a color legend.\n\n    Input structure:\n    - bg = most common color; grey (5) sprites scattered across the grid.\n    - Colored legend shapes (non-bg, non-grey, at least 2×2, not touching the outer border) near grid edge,\n      each with a distinct number of enclosed holes.\n\n    Rule:\n    - Each colored legend shape defines a mapping: hole count → color.\n    - For every grey sprite, count its holes (enclosed bg regions not touching the sprite's bounding-box border).\n    - Recolor the grey sprite to the matching legend color; erase grey distractors with unlisted hole counts.\n\n    Key insight: Shape identity is encoded by topology (number of holes), not geometry or size.\n    \"\"\"\n    g = np.asarray(grid, dtype=int)\n    bg = get_bg(g)\n    grey = 5\n\n    legend = _legend_mapping(g, bg, grey)\n    assert legend, \"legend mapping must be non-empty: grid must contain colored legend shapes\"\n\n    out = g.copy()\n    for pts in components_mask(g == grey, connectivity=4):\n        r0, c0, r1, c1 = bbox_coords(pts)\n        sub = np.zeros((r1 - r0 + 1, c1 - c0 + 1), dtype=bool)\n        for r, c in pts:\n            sub[r - r0, c - c0] = True\n        hc = _hole_count(sub)\n        newc = int(legend[hc]) if hc in legend else bg\n        for r, c in pts:\n            out[r, c] = newc\n\n    return out\n\n# --------------- generator (holes-first organic blob) ---------------\n\nfrom arc_utils import label_mask\nfrom scipy.ndimage import binary_dilation, generate_binary_structure\n\n# -- palette & grid --\nBG = 0\nDIV = 1\nGREY = 5\nGRID_SIZE = 30\nLEGEND_COLORS = [1, 2, 3, 4, 6, 7, 8, 9]\n\n# -- legend panel --\nLEGEND_COUNT_RANGE = (2, 4)         # number of legend entries\nMAX_HOLE_COUNT = 6                  # hole values drawn from range(MAX_HOLE_COUNT)\nPANEL_SIZE_RANGE = (5, 8)           # panel thickness (cross-axis)\nFULL_LAYOUT_MAX_SPAN = 28          # max legend line span for full-row/col layouts\nL_LAYOUT_MAX_SPAN = 24            # max legend line span for L-shaped layouts\nL_LAYOUT_EXTRA_PADDING = 3        # max random padding along the L arm\n\n# -- sprites --\nTOTAL_SPRITES_RANGE = (8, 11)       # total sprites (matches + distractors)\nMAX_DISTRACTORS = 7                 # max distractor sprites\nMAX_EXTRA_PER_LEGEND = 2            # max extra match sprites per legend entry\nSPRITE_RETRIES = 30                 # retries per sprite generation attempt\nSPRITE_AREA_0 = (5, 25)              # (min, max) area for 0-hole sprites\nSPRITE_AREA_LOW_MIN = 8              # min area for 1-2 hole sprites (max = 25+10*h)\n# 3+ hole sprites: min = 10+2*h, max = 20+4*h\nCANVAS_SCALE = 1.2                  # sqrt(area) multiplier for canvas size\nCANVAS_MIN = 5                      # minimum canvas dimension\nCANVAS_PAD = 2                      # padding added to scaled sqrt for canvas\nHOLE_SEED_RADIUS_FACTOR = 0.45      # radius = factor * sqrt(area)\nHOLE_SEED_MIN_RADIUS = 2\nHOLE_SEED_MIN_SEP = 2               # minimum Chebyshev distance between hole seeds\nHOLE_SEED_MARGIN = 2                # margin from canvas edge for hole seeds\nSEAL_ITERS = 5                      # max iterations for sealing forbidden cells\nSPRITE_MAX_H = 12                   # max sprite bbox height\nSPRITE_MAX_W = 18                   # max sprite bbox width\nSPRITE_MAX_ASPECT = 2.5             # max aspect ratio (max_dim / min_dim)\n\n# -- generation --\nGEN_RETRIES = 300                   # outer retries for generate_input()\n\n# 8-connectivity structuring element for dilation\n_STRUCT8 = generate_binary_structure(2, 2)\n\n\n# ---------- legend helpers ----------\n\ndef _legend_span(hole_count: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Width (or height) of a single legend patch along the arrangement axis.\"\"\"\n    return 3 if hole_count == 0 else 2 * hole_count + 1\n\n\ndef _legend_patch(hole_count: int, color: int, arrangement: str) -> np.ndarray:\n    \"\"\"Build a 3xSpan (horizontal) or Spanx3 (vertical) legend patch.\"\"\"\n    span = _legend_span(hole_count)\n    if arrangement == \"horizontal\":\n        patch = np.full((3, span), int(color), dtype=int)\n        if hole_count:\n            patch[1, 1::2] = BG\n    else:\n        patch = np.full((span, 3), int(color), dtype=int)\n        if hole_count:\n            patch[1::2, 1] = BG\n    return patch\n\n\ndef _line_span(legends: list[tuple[int, int]]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Total span of legend patches plus 1-cell gaps between them.\"\"\"\n    return sum(_legend_span(h) for h, _ in legends) + len(legends) - 1\n\n\ndef _choose_legends(arrangement: str, max_span: int) -> list[tuple[int, int]]:\n    \"\"\"Pick 2-4 legends with distinct hole counts that fit within max_span.\"\"\"\n    count = random.randint(*LEGEND_COUNT_RANGE)\n    combos = [holes for holes in itertools.combinations(range(MAX_HOLE_COUNT), count)\n              if sum(_legend_span(h) for h in holes) + count - 1 <= max_span]\n    if not combos:\n        return _choose_legends(arrangement, max_span + 2)\n    holes = list(random.choice(combos))\n    random.shuffle(holes)\n    colors = random.sample(LEGEND_COLORS, count)\n    return list(zip(holes, colors))\n\n\ndef _place_legend_line(\n    grid: np.ndarray, legends: list[tuple[int, int]], arrangement: str, r: int, c: int\n) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Paste legend patches sequentially along the arrangement axis.\"\"\"\n    rr, cc = int(r), int(c)\n    for hole_count, color in legends:\n        patch = _legend_patch(hole_count, color, arrangement)\n        paste(grid, patch, rr, cc)\n        if arrangement == \"horizontal\":\n            cc += patch.shape[1] + 1\n        else:\n            rr += patch.shape[0] + 1\n\n\n# ---------- layout helpers ----------\n\ndef _layout_full_horizontal(grid: np.ndarray, blocked: np.ndarray) -> list[tuple[int, int]]:\n    \"\"\"Place a full-row horizontal divider with legend panel above or below.\"\"\"\n    legends = _choose_legends(\"horizontal\", FULL_LAYOUT_MAX_SPAN)\n    total = _line_span(legends)\n    panel_h = random.randint(*PANEL_SIZE_RANGE)\n    top = random.choice([True, False])\n    c0 = random.randint(1, GRID_SIZE - 1 - total)\n    if top:\n        div_r = panel_h\n        grid[div_r, :] = DIV\n        blocked[: div_r + 1, :] = 9\n        r0 = random.randint(1, panel_h - 4)\n    else:\n        div_r = GRID_SIZE - 1 - panel_h\n        grid[div_r, :] = DIV\ndef generate_input() -> np.ndarray:\n    for _ in range(GEN_RETRIES):\n        try:\n            grid = _gen_attempt()\n        except Exception:\n            grid = None\n        if grid is not None:\n            return grid\n    raise RuntimeError(\"failed to generate e3721c99 input\")\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
